{
  "_comment": [
    "Measured on rbe-west, the lane's own remote executors (instance oss), on",
    "2026-10-09: two `bazel test //cmd/bd:bd_proxied_test",
    "--config=doltserver-proxied --nocache_test_results` runs, one against the",
    "then-committed 30-shard block and one against a 40-shard repack, so every",
    "discovered test ran exactly once per run, with the lane's -test.parallel=4",
    "and GOMAXPROCS=4. Both passed.",
    "",
    "Each value is a top-level test's serial-equivalent cost: the sum of the",
    "<testcase time> of every leaf test under it (a subtest with no subtests of",
    "its own; the test itself when it has none), each leaf averaged over the",
    "two runs. It is NOT <testsuite time>, which the previous (local) capture",
    "used: for a t.Parallel test that attribute runs from the test's first RUN",
    "line to its last PASS line, so it also counts the time the test sat paused",
    "behind its shard's other tests. That made a cheap test that happened to",
    "wait look as heavy as the shard, which is why the previous 30-shard block,",
    "packed to ~360s per shard on paper, ran 38-286s per shard in CI. Leaves,",
    "not direct subtests, because a parallel group's own <testcase time> is 0.",
    "",
    "A shard's remote wall time came out at about 0.3x its packed cost (four",
    "subtests run at once): correlation 0.90 over the 30-shard run (19,224",
    "cost-seconds, 5,671 shard-seconds of wall time); the 40-shard run's",
    "shards ran 71-162s, apart from one that held two then-unsplit tests whose",
    "cost the first capture had missed.",
    "",
    "The cost is almost all `bd init --proxied-server` against the shared dolt",
    "sql-server: each init issues ~2,000 statements (81 DOLT_COMMITs) and costs",
    "the server ~6-12 CPU-seconds, and most subtests run one init. A top-level",
    "test with ~20 single-init subtests therefore cost 600-920 and ran for up",
    "to ~350s alone, which no shard count can pack under that. The fifteen",
    "heaviest were split into two or three top-level functions",
    "(TestProxiedServerUpdate, -UpdateB, -UpdateC, ...); a split function's",
    "entry is the sum of the leaves it now holds.",
    "",
    "`seconds_per_init_fallback` is the sum of all costs over the sum of all",
    "inits (discover_inits_cost()), used only for a test with no entry yet.",
    "",
    "Regenerate the same way: fresh remote runs of the target, then sum each",
    "top-level test's leaf <testcase time>s from every shard's",
    "bazel-testlogs/cmd/bd/bd_proxied_test/shard_*/test.xml."
  ],
